# A guest throws the box onto the open floor. It meets nothing that is not static, so its flight
# goes back to the host when it sleeps under either flight_end and either authority: a return at
# rest, and the grab before it a switch from rest.
scenario return_rest
scene two_chars_item
seed 17
guests 1
settle 6s
light_mass 20kg

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 10ms loss 1%

p1 walk box
p1 grab box as lift
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 5 0.2 3 speed 4 as throw

expect result lift granted
expect result throw done
expect agree_at_rest 5cm
expect no_stuck
# Derived: both sides hold one rest pose when the body goes back. The guest's rest state carries its
# pose to the bit, the host's copy rests on it or, within the second layer's dead zone (1 cm), goes
# on from its own pose, and a copy in the rest hold takes a state within a copy-grid step (3.4 mm)
# of its pose without moving: no picture moves more than the dead zone, 1 cm, in the window.
expect return_jump.max <= 1cm
# The host's picture and the thrower's were both handed back: 2 windows.
expect return_jump.count >= 2
# Derived: a grab takes over from the pose the claimant shows, its copy of the box at rest, so the
# host's copy starts within the dead zone of its own body: 1 cm.
expect switch_jump.max <= 1cm
